What is adapted from it here: the pdf skill
(internal/controlplane/clientcli/skills/pdf/): its SKILL.md, references/forms.md
and the scripts in scripts/. Changed: the interpreter block is `python` only
(the Bots' documents environment) and the scripts are named where the skill is
installed, ~/.agents/skills/pdf/scripts; Hermes's own frontmatter fields and
tool names give way to the Agent Skills fields and pi's tools (bash, read,
write); OCR (references/ocr-extraction.md, scripts/extract_pymupdf.py,
scripts/extract_marker.py), nano-pdf editing (references/nano-pdf-editing.md)
and tests/ are left out with every mention of them, in SKILL.md, forms.md,
pdf_read.py, pdf_page_image.py and pdf_form_layout.py.

What is learned from it, with no code of it copied: how `hypomnema skills
install` puts a whole skill folder in place and leaves an edited copy alone,
from tools/skills_sync.py (dir_hash, _is_runtime_cache, _replace_skill_dir).
